# Trivy misconfiguration suppressions for this repo (intentional, documented).

# AVD-DS-0002 — the worker image builds on the shared worker-bridge base,
# which runs as root by design today (same as aws-s3-bucket): the runtime user
# is governed by the agent's worker pod securityContext, not by a USER
# directive here. Revisit when the bridge ships a non-root variant.
AVD-DS-0002

# The deployment module creates the account with
# public_network_access_enabled = true and a network rule whose default_action
# is "Allow" (bypass: AzureServices). That is a documented product decision —
# see "The account is reachable from the public internet" in
# azure-blob-storage/README.md — not an oversight: private endpoints and
# network ACLs are out of scope for this version, and access still requires a
# valid SAS with public blob access disabled.
#
# Add the AVD ID here once a scan reports it. A guessed ID suppresses nothing
# and reads as though a real finding was reviewed.
